# tools/e/encoding_pem_witness.rish -- PEM (RFC 7468) authored in pure Rye as a composition: the labelled armor a key, certificate, or signed
# carry wears as text (a -----BEGIN LABEL----- line, the payload in standard Base64 wrapped at 64 characters a line, a -----END LABEL----- line),
# proven against a reproducible RFC-4648-anchored known-answer with a round-trip and a second independent deframer (encoding - the serialization
# sibling of Season G - Cryptography).
#
# Season: encoding -- the text-form sibling of the crypto library, beside base64.rye and base58check.rye. This rung authors NO new base
# conversion: it composes one already-GREEN stone -- the standard-Base64 rendering from encoding/base64.rye (RFC 4648, parity-GREEN against
# std.base64) -- and adds only the RFC 7468 label framing and the 64-character line wrap a real key or certificate carries, so a keeper reads
# what a block holds at a glance and a parser finds exactly the bytes between the markers.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (the wave that seats the Rye-first spine).
# Clean-room: the -----BEGIN/END LABEL----- framing and the 64-character wrap are RFC 7468's own public convention; the composition is ours,
# standing on our own parity-GREEN Base64 primitive (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# encoding/pem.rye writes -----BEGIN <label>----- , the Base64 body wrapped at 64 characters a line, and -----END <label>----- ; decode
# locates the markers for the requested label, gathers the Base64 between them (skipping the wrap whitespace), and Base64-decodes it,
# refusing BadLabel when the block does not claim the requested label. Parity is proven at selftest against the reproducible known-answer
# ("foobar" under "GRAIN TEST" -> -----BEGIN GRAIN TEST----- ‖ Zm9vYmFy ‖ -----END GRAIN TEST-----, since Zm9vYmFy is RFC 4648 §10's published
# Base64 of "foobar"), a round-trip across payloads 0..96 bytes whose body lines never exceed 64 characters recovered by a second independent
# deframer, and the guards: a wrong label refuses BadLabel, a bad character BadChar, a too-small destination DestTooSmall. Purely local -- no
# key, no network, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/e/encoding_pem_witness.rish

say "encoding-pem: Language EN — PEM is the armor a key, a certificate, or a signed carry wears when it travels as text: a -----BEGIN LABEL----- line, the payload rendered in standard Base64 and wrapped at 64 characters a line, and a -----END LABEL----- line to close it. It is the exact form an Ed25519 key or a signature is pasted into a config file, mailed between two hands, or committed beside its code — the shape openssl prints and every TLS stack reads. This module composes one already-GREEN rung and authors none of its own base arithmetic."
say "encoding-pem: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively: encode writes the BEGIN line, the Base64 body in 64-character lines, and the END line; decode locates the markers for the requested label, gathers every Base64 character between them, and decodes it — returning bytes only from a block that claims the requested label, so a block is never read as something it does not say it is."
say "encoding-pem: Lens TAME — no new base conversion: the rendering is the GREEN encoding/base64.rye, proven byte-for-byte against std.base64. Bounded payload (max_der_bytes) and label (max_label_len), contract asserts on every function, buffer-length checked before the first write. Parity holds against the reproducible RFC-4648-anchored known-answer AND a round-trip across payloads 0..96 bytes whose body lines never exceed 64 characters, recovered by a second independent deframer; a wrong label refuses BadLabel, a bad character BadChar, a too-small destination DestTooSmall — each before a partial result escapes. Purely local — no key, no network, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "encoding/bin/pem"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p encoding/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build encoding/pem.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "encoding-pem: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "encoding/bin/pem.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "encoding-pem: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "encoding-pem: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN encoding-pem' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "encoding-pem: selftest did not print the GREEN encoding-pem line"
